ly ill patient.</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>1981</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>515</fpage><lpage>518</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7238059</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mirvis</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Tobin</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kostrubiak</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Belzberg</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Thoracic computed tomography in detecting occult disease in			 critically ill patients.</article-title><source>AJR Am J Roentgenol</source><year>1987</year><volume>148</volume><fpage>685</fpage><lpage>689</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3493649</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Voggenreiter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Aufmkolk</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Majetschak</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Efficiency of chest computed tomography in critically ill multiple			 trauma patients.</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>27</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><article-title>Guidelines for the transfer of critically ill patients.</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>1993</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>931</fpage><lpage>937</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8080468</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burtnyk</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Secondary transportation of critically ill people: implications for			 nurses and the need for specialist training. </article-title><source>Intens Crit Care Nurs</source><year>1992</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>234</fpage><lpage>239</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gervais</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Eberle</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Konietzke</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hennes</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dick</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of blood gases of ventilated patients during			 transport.</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>1987</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>761</fpage><lpage>763</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3475193</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heinrichs</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Mertzlufft</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Dick</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Accuracy of delivered versus preset minute ventilation of portable			 emergency ventilators.</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>1989</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>682</fpage><lpage>685</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2736931</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barton</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Tuttle-Newhall</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Szalados</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Portable power supply for continuous mechanical ventilation during			 intrahospital transport of critically ill patients with ARDS.</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>1997</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>560</fpage><lpage>563</lpage><pub-id pub-id-